Technique: FE workflow: (1) Guess solution (try f=0,x,-x,kx,kx+c,x^2). (2) Substitute x=y=0 to find f(0). (3) One variable=0 to simplify. (4) Force cancellation by setting arguments equal. (5) Swap x,y for new equation. (6) Replace x with f(t) if bijective. Reduce to Cauchy form when possible.
Question: Find all f:R->R with f(x+y)+f(x-y) = 2f(x)+2f(y) for all x,y.
Answer: x=y=0: f(0)+f(0)=4f(0), so f(0)=0. y=x: f(2x)+f(0)=2f(x)+2f(x), so f(2x)=4f(x). This suggests f(x)=cx^2. Verify: c(x+y)^2+c(x-y)^2 = c(x^2+2xy+y^2+x^2-2xy+y^2) = 2cx^2+2cy^2 = 2f(x)+2f(y). For uniqueness: set g(x)=f(x)/f(1), then g(1)=1, g is continuous (if assumed), and g(r)=r^2 for all rationals by induction. With continuity, f(x)=cx^2. Without continuity, pathological solutions exist.

